>> title: Club Sandwich
>> category: Sandwiches & Rolls
>> tags: turkey, bacon, toast, sandwich, lunch
>> counters: Diner, Deli
>> aka: club, clubhouse sandwich, triple decker, turkey club, club house
>> servings: 2
>> time: 20 min

>> step: fry until flat and crisp, 8 min
Fry @thick-cut bacon{6%slices} in a #skillet{} over medium heat ~fry{8%min}, turning and pressing, until it is flat and brittle.

>> step: toast all six slices, 3 min
Toast @white sandwich bread{6%slices} ~toast{3%min}, three slices to a sandwich — the middle slice is what makes it a club rather than a large sandwich.

>> step: spread every inside face
Spread @mayonnaise{3%Tbs}(45 mL) over every inside face of @&(~1)toast{}, right to the edges.

>> step: stack two decks, pick the quarters, cut both diagonals
Layer @&(~3)bacon{}, @roast turkey{6%oz}(170 g; sliced thin), @beefsteak tomato{1%large}(in 1/4-in slices), @iceberg lettuce{4%leaves}, @kosher salt{1/4%tsp} and @black pepper{1/4%tsp} across @&(~1)dressed toast{} in two decks — turkey below, bacon and tomato above — then run a pick through each quarter and cut corner to corner both ways.
